ements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a84392ea1475add4804237f151dcb4b4dd499a8c7c1732cd6f290b7795796c85"} {"question" "q-177660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f92