e matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The number of rows in $A$ is not the same as the number of columns. So, it's not a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Note that\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\cdot A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not a square matrix, our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a84392ea1475add4804237f151dcb4b4dd499a8c7c1732cd6f290b7795796c85"} {"question" "q-177667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the statements"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is a square matrix\n- $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a84392ea1475add4804237f151dcb4b4dd499a8c7c1732cd6f290b7795796c85"} {"question" "q-177662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-177662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f7025b9d1b7674fbf248fafde36bfa34195f924d7f7bfa93883cdf0a10d0a06"} {"question" "q-84255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse of the orthogonal matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy